        "47": `## Key Concept
**Method of Moments** — Method-of-moments estimators by equating population and sample moments. *(Ref: Casella & Berger, Statistical Inference, 2nd ed., Ch. 7)*

## Solution
1. For Gamma, \\( E(X) = \\alpha\\beta \\) and \\( \\text{Var}(X) = \\alpha\\beta^2 \\).
2. MOM equations: \\( \\alpha\\beta = \\bar{X} \\) and \\( \\alpha\\beta^2 = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum (X_i - \\bar{X})^2 = s^2 \\).
3. Then \\( \\beta = s^2/\\bar{X} \\) and \\( \\alpha = \\bar{X}/\\beta = \\bar{X}^2/s^2 \\).
4. This matches (b).

**Answer: (a)**

## Alternative Method
Set \\(E(X^k)=m_k\\) and solve; for Gamma, \\(\\hat{\\beta}=s^2/\\bar{x}\\), \\(\\hat{\\alpha}=\\bar{x}^2/s^2\\).

## Exam Trick
> ISS tip: For \\(U(a,b)\\): \\(\\hat{a}=\\bar{x}-s\\sqrt{3}\\), \\(\\hat{b}=\\bar{x}+s\\sqrt{3}\\) (standard MOM on uniform).

## Common Pitfall
Equating the wrong moment order, or algebra errors solving for \\(\\theta\\).`,
