        "71": `## Key Concept
**Indian Official Statistical System** — MoSPI/NSO coordination, decentralized collection by ministries and states, surveys vs administrative data. *(Ref: MoSPI, Indian Statistical System; UN Fundamental Principles of Official Statistics)*

## Solution
1. Merchandise Trade Statistics are compiled by the DGCI&S using data from shipping bills and bills of entry.
2. Since this data is a by-product of the regulatory and customs process, it is classified as **administrative statistics**.

**Answer: (b)**

## Alternative Method
Eliminate options by agency ownership: MoSPI/NSO, RGI, Labour Bureau, line ministries — one wrong pairing falsifies the code.

## Exam Trick
> ISS tip: India = decentralized (Centre + States + subjects). CSO/NSO coordinates; RGI \\(\\neq\\) sole census agency.

## Common Pitfall
Attributing all censuses to RGI — Agriculture and Economic Censuses are conducted by other ministries.`,
        "72": `## Key Concept
**Agricultural Statistics in India** — Crop output via area × yield (CCE); Agriculture Census operational holdings. *(Ref: Ministry of Agriculture; MoSPI)*

## Solution
1. The output of agricultural crops in India is estimated using the formula: **Production = Area \\( \\times \\) Yield**.
2. The area is obtained through land records, and the yield (productivity) is estimated through sample surveys called Crop Cutting Experiments (CCE).

**Answer: (b)**

## Alternative Method
Eliminate options by agency ownership: MoSPI/NSO, RGI, Labour Bureau, line ministries — one wrong pairing falsifies the code.

## Exam Trick
> ISS tip: Match survey to conducting agency — NFHS (MoHFW), PLFS/TUS (MoSPI), Population Census (RGI), CES (NSO).

## Common Pitfall
Selecting "all of the above" without verifying each statement — SDGs were adopted by UN General Assembly, not formulated solely by UNDP.`,
        "73": `## Key Concept
**Index Number Theory** — Laspeyres, Paasche, Fisher ideal index; bias, base revision, and economic interpretation. *(Ref: SPIES, Official Statistics; CSO/WPI/CPI manuals)*

## Solution
1. As per the current series, the base years are: CPI-IW (2016), CPI-Combined (2012), and WPI (2011–12).
2. The **CPI for Agricultural Labourers (AL) and Rural Labourers (RL)** still uses the old base of **1986–87**.
3. Therefore, 2015 is not correctly matched.

**Answer: (c)**

## Alternative Method
Laspeyres uses base quantities; Paasche uses current quantities; Fisher \\(= \\sqrt{L \\times P}\\) satisfies time-reversal and factor-reversal tests.

## Exam Trick
> ISS tip: Laspeyres \\(\\rightarrow\\) upward bias; base year must be revised periodically. Fisher ideal \\(\\approx\\) geometric mean of L and P.

## Common Pitfall
Swapping Laspeyres and Paasche weight periods; or claiming Fisher uses only base-year weights.`,
